  "id": "nondirectional-test",
  "term": "nondirectional test",
  "definition": "A nondirectional test is a significance test that evaluates whether a result differs from the null hypothesis in either direction, not just one specified direction. It uses a two-tailed probability, counting outcomes that are as extreme or more extreme on both the higher and lower sides of the null value.",
